FYI

xanthian.

The NetHack adventures of Kibble, Chaotic Male Orcish Wizard.

    As a new "get more varied bones files" strategy
    this game, bones files, once unused, are being
    moved by hand out of the way of more bones files
    being dropped, a lot of trouble for a 1/3rd
    chance, but it's my own fault for backing up and
    reusing bones files to keep a rich variety of
    them.

Kibble came into the world plain, healthy, and
dextrous, as smart as any orc, but lacking exercise
and most unwise:

Kibble the Evoker St:9 Dx:16 Co:14 In:16 Wi:8 Ch:10 Chaotic
Dlvl:1 $:0 HP:11(11) Pw:7(7) AC:9 Xp:1/0 T:4

His faithful kitten Purrball I at his side, his
starting kit a modest one, but nice as wizard's kits
go:

  a wand of locking (0:5)
  an uncursed ring of see invisible
  an uncursed ring of polymorph control
  a potion of holy water
  an uncursed potion of water
  an uncursed potion of restore ability
  an uncursed spellbook of extra healing
  a blessed spellbook of force bolt
  an uncursed scroll of destroy armor
  an uncursed scroll of enchant armor
  a blessed scroll of identify
  an uncursed +0 cloak of magic resistance
  a blessed +1 quarterstaff

The wand is a waste in the early game, the rings are
junk, but the holy water and blessed ID will be
useful, and extra healing, when he levels up, will
perhaps save his life on and off. We'd like to both
burn the enchant armor and keep the holy water, so
the restore ability must go, or some other junk
potion, at the first fountain.

Two cream pies in room 1:1 improve the food
situation for now. A Newt, standing just outside a
closed door, becomes Kibble's first victim, dropping
no corpse, and the battle for dungeon supremacy is
on.

    Where possible, wizards should leave everything
    _but_ newts to their pet in the early game; the
    chance of a mild buzz from a newt, though low,
    makes them the sole exception to avoiding combat
    where possible to keep XP and XL down.

In room 1:2, a runed bow is left to lie, a sink left
carefully unkicked; now is not the time.

Room 1:3 contains the stairs down, so Kibble quickly
ducks down them to map the area around the stairs so
that they will be easy to locate if a trap door
incident occurs. [This is a game, after all.]

Room 2:1 contains a Jade Ring, grabbed, and a
fountain, remembered for later. Kibble climbs back
up the stairs to resume exploring level 1 at room
1:3.

In the hallway outside room 1:4, a Lichen is left to
Purrball I's attention, and luckily drops a corpse,
added to Kibble's food-in-knapsack.

Room 1:4 contains no floor goodies, but does contain
a fountain, useful later perhaps.

Room 1:5 contains a treasure indeed, an altar to
Anhur, the cruel chaotic god whose service dominates
Kibble's life!

It is too soon to pray, only T:127, but a drop of
all un-B/U/C IDd items shows the Jade Ring to be a
dangerous, cursed one, the food uncursed as usual.

Oh, well, cursed items are good cat dissuaders.

Grabbing back the dropped items, Kibble continues
exploring Dlvl:1.

Room 1:6 is large but empty of goods and of dungeon
dressing, except perhaps for hidden traps.

A Newt is seen just as Kibble departs room 1:6, so
he returns to combat it, and easily slays it bare
handed, but it drops no corpse. Strike two on Newt
corpses!

Outside room 1:6, Kibble finds a boulder with a
hallway that allows turning around at both ends, and
an alternate path to reach the other side of the
boulder in case an immovable monster shows up behind
it, so he stops for some exercise, pushing the
boulder back and forth half a dozen times. Purrball
I, of course, _insists_ on being on the wrong side
of the boulder most of the time, so the mantra "move
your butt, you stupid cat" begins to be heard at a
mutter in the dungeon's first level. The hallway is
a nice long one, allowing 22 pushes before a turn
around, so Kibble quickly works up a glowing sweat,
and decides to continue exploring Dlvl:1.

Aha! Better and better, room 1:7 contains a floor
litter velvet spellbook, and with an aligned altar,
one holy water already, and another clear potion in
the starting kit, blessing stuff is a "mere" matter
of finding junk potions and a pick-axe. Of course,
having the velvet spellbook being bait for a
beartrap does nothing good for Kibble's mood. 22
turns of struggle get Kibble free, only to step on a
magic trap and be made blind, the very next turn!

Grrrrr, RNG, go pick on someone your own size!

Stopping to type reminds the player that searching
Right Now would be an excellent idea, and sure
enough, two monsters are found. An attempt to #chat
with the one less likely to be the pet cat Purrball
I gets no response, and a quick force bolt to the
body kills whatever attacker that was, something
worth 4 XP, while Kibble loses HP only down to 9.
The formation of room 1:7, only two grid cells high,
leaves access to a possible corpse a way to be left
behind two traps in a cull-de-sac, so Kibble steps
off the magic trap _away_ from the possible corpse,
disarms the beartrap, still while blind, in a single
try, then steps back across the now safe passage to
check for a corpse, but there was none.

Probably to the far edge of Dlvl:1, but needing to
stall to recover from blindness, Kibble searches for
a possible doorway, finds none, but does recover his
sight as expected.

A peaceful goblin is encountered, when exploration
is resumed the other direction, but "peaceful" means
little to the forces of Chaos, so Purrball I is sent
on ahead to check that goblin for orcish knives or
orcish helms, both possibly valuable at this point
in the game to an under-equipped wizard.

It had both, and Purrball I was a bit slow-moving,
so away goes one conduct as cannibal-Kibble eats a
fellow member of the orcish race.

Purrball I outraces Kibble to one Newt, Kibble kills
another, but neither drops a corpse, and Kibble is
now at Xp:1/7.

Turn 600 passes, and Kibble's exercise is rewarded
with a boost to St:10, just as the local gym is
being passed. Time to shove a boulder again!

That is quickly slowed by a monster popping up on
the far side of the boulder, and in the run around
the alternate path, _another_ magic trap, in the
same room with Anhur's altar, is tripped over,
luckily only sending a shiver down Kibble's spine.

Also, an entrance to a teleport trap, sure sign of a
vault somewhere, is found along the way in room 1:6.

The monster turns out to be a kobold zombie, which
Purrball I quickly dispatches, along with a lichen
encountered on the way, a corpseless one. And in the
case, the exercise hallway had become jammed, with
_two_ corpseless Newts between Kibble and boulder;
Xp:1/9.

During exercise, besides being massively in the way,
Kibble kills a stray sewer rat.

After some more exercise, Kibble returns to the
altar the long way around, finding two peaceful
goblins along the way, both of which Purrball I
eventually eats, neither of which are carrying
anything. Kibble finds the orcish helm from the
earlier goblin to be blessed, puts it on, but it is
unenchanted, provides just a single AC boost.

Good luck mixed with bad playing result in a
fountain turning into a set of pools close by the
altar room, as Kibble #dips the potion of restore
ability prior to doing a water prayer, but an
unnoticed orcish helm which is being worn and so
doesn't drop with the rest of the pre-swim goodies
rusts, and now it provides no AC boost, just falling
rock protection.

Still, Kibble now has two clear potions (besides his
one holy water) to put on the altar while an
upcoming food prayer is done, which will let some
stuff be blessed soon. Sure enough, a bit later, a
content stomach and two blue glowing potions.

One attempt to read the velvet spellbook finds it
"difficult", so rather than risk problems, Kibble
stops studying to #dip it, and reads it again
blessed, only to find that it is Wizard Lock, not
the spell of ones dreams!

Another potion of holy water is burned to bless the
scroll of enchant armor, and Kibble's cloak is now
at +2, AC:7 (ugh).

With no container yet, and no zorkmids yet, and
lousy AC, altar camping is right out, it is time for
Kibble to go explore more dungeon, carefully, to
find and drag a container back for altar top use. He
lightens his load by dropping spellbooks, and the
cursed Jade Ring as a cat-dissuader, and heads for
Dlvl:2.

But just as he is about to step off the altar, two
jackels enter the room; one drops a corpse and a
leash, and Kibble is now satiated (oops, but
sacrificing it would have been a waste of time a
couple of turns after a food prayer), has dropped
everything but armor and weapons, keeps the leash
after testing it to be uncursed (it may come in
handy in robbing a shop), is now Xp:1/11, and headed
once again downwards.

Room 2:2 yields up a maple wand and 11 zorkmids,
plus a plague of grid bugs easily handled by
Purrball I. The maple wand, when engrave tested,
turns out to be Light, not a favorite, and Kibble
explores onward.

Oh, yummy, somewhere on Dlvl:2, a shopkeeper is
fussying about shoplifters!

Room 2:3 is much nicer, producing another scroll of
enchant armor, worth carrying back to the altar to
test, bless if needed, and apply once more to the
cloak of magic resistance.

On the way back to the stairs up, via a different
hallway, a scroll is found in the hallway outside a
room, almost certainly Teleportation. Back at the
altar, it tests blessed, while the enchant armor is
uncursed. Oh, now that was nice, the enchant armor,
once blessed with the last current potion of holy
water, brought the cloak to +5, with a long silver
glow and a warning violent vibration! Now AC:4, we
won't be enchanting the cloak any further!

The scroll of teleportation, being of tactical use
in battle, is added to the carry-along kit, and
Kibble heads back down to further explore Dlvl:2,
but not before hearing the footsteps of a vault
guard somewhere on Dlvl:1, a reason to go to Mines
looking for an unneeded pick-axe.

While Kibble was in communion with Anhur, Purrball I
was beating up on some poor goblin, so Kibble trades
in his blessed rusty orcish helm on a shiny new
uncursed one, for AC:3.

A quick click back to tiles mode shows that Purrball
I, despite all this mayhem, is still a kitten at
heart. Phooey.

Room 2:4 yields 109 zorkmids, but with a kobold
zombie in slow pursuit. Where _is_ that cat?

Room 2:5 is large but empty.

Room 2:6 contains zorkmids, too, but a trapdoor
along the way finds Kibble in room 4:1; oops!
That room contains 9 zorkmids and a papaya.

Room 4:2 contains some stairs, but stairs _down_,
and a lockpick, a welcome acquisition indeed, as it
allows quieter exploration without kicking down
doors. A quick duck down to room 5:1 finds it
mid-dungeon level, and empty.

Room 4:3 coughs up 45 zorkmids, now $:174.

Room 4:4 contains a peaceful goblin, cat chow for
later, and the stairs down to what must be Mines
1/5.

Ducking down for a look, Kibble finds himself in the
middle of a room and with one Gnome in sight, runs
right back up the stairs, on the "run away, live to
watch your pet fight another day" plan.

On the way back to find some up-stairs, Kibble finds
a gas spoor and a hostile goblin by room 4:2, but
continues to retreat rather than fight alone.

Room 4:5 contains another gas spoor and a sink, and
the hostile orc is now visible in the room behind.

Room 4:6 yields 73 zorkmids.

Room 4:7 yields a dark blue spellbook and a scroll
labeled ZELGO MER. The sound of a vault guard is
heard, and immediately afterwards a floor engraving
leads to a closet containing another teleport trap
to a vault. Kibble _really_ wants a pick-axe now!

With a reverse of path to room 4:8, the pursuing
goblin catches up, and Kibble has no choice but to
force bolt it. Xp:1/17. It drops a sling, which
Kibble leaves where it fell.

Room 4:8 provides 85 zorkmids.

Blindly blundering into a Lichen, Kibble kills it
unintentionally, and is now Xp:2/21. He grabs its
corpse for emergency noshing; Kibble is a long way
from his home altar!

Room 4:9 is empty, and all these tiny rooms still
leave 1/4th of the level empty!

Room 4:10 contains the stairs up, at long last, and
a statue of a Lichen, useless dungeon dressing this
high up in the dungeon.

A tardy check shows that Mines 1/4 is going to be a
bones level; ugh, Kibble needed an _uncomplicated_
way to improve AC and find a pick-axe, this will be
neither.

Some perhaps wasted searching when a vault is know
to exist on Dlvl:4 and the search was toward its
most likely location, merely finds an iguana
snipping after Kibble, who retreats upstairs rather
than fight.

Room 3:1 is rife with goodies, ring, wand, scroll,
stairs down. The ring is agate, the wand is pine,
the scroll is labeled KERNOD WEL. Kibble needs
another stairs up to find Purrball I, only maybe
still tame when he returns.

Large room 3:2 provides a food ration and 117
zorkmids. Now at least Kibble has a way to retame
his pet if needed.

Room 3:3 provides a scroll labeled FOOBIE BLETCH,
56 zorkmids, and a blue gem. Kibble gloats a moment
over his enormous wealth, $:505 and a probable
worthless piece of blue glass.

A tardily remembered engraving test of the pine wand
finds that it slows down floor bugs, sure sign of a
Slow Monster wand, one of the better life-saving
wands the Dungeons of Doom hold!

Room 3:4 holds only a statue of a Gecko.

Opening a door into the face of a jackel, Kibble is
now Xp:2/22, and notices that while the promotion to
level 2 was generous with HP:20(20), it was stingy
with Pw:4(9), so a second force bolt spell is not
immediately available.

The jackel had a delicious friend, Xp:2/23, and just
as force bolt was again castable, luckily.

Short of PW, Kibble shifts weapons to an orcish
dagger, to exercise dagger skills, and takes on a
yellow mold blocking a doorway with many a stagger,
but the hallway limits his stumbling to harmless
folly, and eventually he succeeds, while his PW
builds back to Pw:6(9) unnoticed.

Room 3:2 also holds a pit, for some reason already
known to Kibble.

Kibble passes and ignores an acid blob in a hallway,
finds 21 zorkmids and a dark potion in room 3:5.

Room 3:6 contains zorkmids and a potion, but Kibble
can't stop to gather loot, a Gecko is in hot
pursuit; luckily this room also holds the stairs up.

Unexplored room 2:7 contains 65 zorkmids, a
fountain, and of course the stairs down. Since the
door back toward Purrball I's likely location stands
open, Kibble decides to explore in the other
direction, leaving the problem of reunion in the
paws of his much-swifter-than-he cat.

Lucky thing, too, for there he finds the harbingered
shop, a strange 11x2 room 2:8 with _three_ tripe
rations among its delicatessen fare! Quick, Kibble,
grab them before the cat arrives!

Kibble entered the shop with $:591, and the shop's
entire goods only cost 470 zorkmids, time to drop
cash, buy and dash until a certain credit cloning
cat is located.

Marching cross-dungeon to room 2:6, home of the trap
door, Purrball I is found, still tame, and the 61
zorkmids unreached earlier in room 2:6 is added to
Kibble's trove, most of it, just now, sitting on
Tjiwidej's shop floor. Kibble is hungry, will soon
be weak, wants to pray for food rather than eat some
of his credit cloning stash. Time for a return to
the altar, since one purchase in the shop was a
clear potion!

A quick trip to the altar and back leaves Kibble
with _two_ holy waters, which the shopkeeper is
happy to buy at 50z each, speeding the credit
cloning quite a bit, one clear potion picked up
along the way was already blessed, and a comfortable
tummy. The shopkeeper in room 2:8 is ready to be
bilked by a wizard and his trusty cat.

The dark potion is uninteresting to Tjiwidej, making
it non-fruit juice, non-booze, Kibble thinks.

After one cycle of credit cloning, with the leash
used to keep Purrball near the gold, cash-on-floor
is up to 1128 zorkmids. Whee. Stinker Purrball I ate
a fortune cookie, despite that I piled veggies on
top of it, though.

